# docs/ IS TRACKED as of 2026-07-26 (FULL_AUDIT_2 P1).
#
# It used to be blanket-ignored, which meant the whole design set, every audit,
# and all the verification evidence existed on exactly one machine with no
# backup — for a project whose security claims rest on "it was actually
# checked", the evidence trail is the asset.
#
# It was made safe to track first, not assumed to be: the prod test-account
# password, a personal device UDID, the personal account handles and the preview
# hostname were all moved out to `.env.asc` (ignored by `.*env*` above) and the
# directory re-scanned for credential-shaped strings, key material and private
# addresses. Anything genuinely secret belongs in `.env.asc`, never here.
#
# What remains and is a JUDGEMENT CALL rather than an oversight: Apple team ID
# G2KBQH7KWT, the APNs key IDs and the ASC resource id. Those identify the
# account but are not credentials — the team id ships inside the app binary
# anyway, and an APNs key id is useless without the .p8.
#
# Re-scan before adding new docs. Git history is not undoable.
#
# Root-level markdown stays local (build prompts and scratch notes).
/*.md
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md

# Local verification captures — may contain real message content.
screenshots/

# Playwright MCP screenshots / traces (local verification)
.playwright-mcp/
*-mobile.png
*-desktop.png
m?-*.png

# App Store Connect API private keys — never commit
*.p8
.match.env
asc_api_key.json
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
